# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values. .env.local is never committed.
# Both Supabase values are public by design: the URL only says where the project is, and the publishable key
# identifies the project without granting power. The database rules (supabase/waitlist.sql and
# supabase/workflows.sql) decide what a visitor or a signed-in person may do. Never put a service_role or
# sb_secret_ key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or anywhere in this project.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# Optional: the site's address once it has a domain, used for link previews.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# Optional, SECRET. Lets "Preview plan" use an AI model run by Groq to write the plan. Without it the keyword preview is used.
# Server only: never put NEXT_PUBLIC_ in front of it. Get one at https://console.groq.com/keys (it starts with gsk_)
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional, SECRET. Lets a "Look something up" step set to Linear read YOUR open Linear tasks after you press Approve on the
# Runs page (read-only). Server only: never put NEXT_PUBLIC_ in front of it. Get one in Linear: workspace name, Settings,
# Security & access, Personal API keys, New API key. It starts with lin_api_
# LINEAR_API_KEY=

# Optional, SECRET. The "Connect Linear" button (so each person connects their own Linear with one click). One-time set-up by the
# owner, explained on the Connections page. Server only: never put NEXT_PUBLIC_ in front of any of these.
# CONNECTIONS_KEY: a secret that locks each person's saved connection. Make one with: npm run secret
# LINEAR_CLIENT_ID and LINEAR_CLIENT_SECRET: from Linear, Settings, API, OAuth applications (your own Hushwork app).
# CONNECTIONS_KEY=
# LINEAR_CLIENT_ID=
# LINEAR_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional, SECRET. The "Connect Google" button (Google Calendar, read-only). One-time set-up by the owner, explained on the
# Connections page. GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET come from Google Cloud (APIs & Services, Credentials, OAuth client ID).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional, SECRET. "More apps" (17 apps such as Todoist, Notion, GitHub, Slack, and the email, Slack, GitHub, Todoist, Calendar and Notion actions)
# through Composio (composio.dev, free to start). Sign up, open Settings, Project Settings, API Keys, and copy the PROJECT API key (it starts
# with ak_; a key starting ck_ or uak_ is a different kind and will not work). Server only: never put NEXT_PUBLIC_ in front of it.
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=

# Optional, SECRET. SCHEDULED RUNS (a workflow that runs by itself, for example every weekday at 9am). They need a clock calling
# /api/cron/tick about every minute, which only works while Hushwork is online: see docs/deploy.md. Server only: never put NEXT_PUBLIC_ in
# front of either one.
# CRON_SECRET: the clock's password. Make one with: npm run secret cron
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: Supabase's all-access key (Dashboard, Project Settings, API Keys, the SECRET key). It ignores the privacy rules, so
# it is used only for scheduled runs and Delete my account. Treat it like a bank password.
# CRON_SECRET=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

